# Running .NET tests

Always run tests against the **relevant test project** `.csproj`, never the whole solution.

```bash
dotnet test \
  --tl:off \
  -clp:ErrorsOnly \
  src/Ape.Modules/Ape.Module.CuasEvaluation/Tests/Ape.Module.CuasEvaluation.Tests.csproj
```

Use the test project next to the library: `src/Ape.Core/Tests/` or `src/Ape.Modules/Ape.Module.<Name>/Tests/`.

Use quiet MSBuild/terminal logging so the output stays readable:

```bash
dotnet test \
  --tl:off \
  -clp:ErrorsOnly \
  src/Ape.Modules/Ape.Module.Something/Tests/Ape.Module.Something.Tests.csproj
```

- `--tl:off` — disable the terminal logger
- `-clp:ErrorsOnly` — MSBuild console logger, errors only

To run a single test or class, add `--filter`:

```bash
dotnet test \
  --tl:off \
  -clp:ErrorsOnly \
  --filter FullyQualifiedName~TypeOrMethodName \
  src/Ape.Modules/Ape.Module.Something/Tests/Ape.Module.Something.Tests.csproj
```

Do not add `-v detailed`, `--logger "console;verbosity=detailed"`, or other verbose flags unless the user asks.
